    "question": {
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "What are the pivot columns of the matrix $B,$ given by\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$\n",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we need to convert $B$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} && R_{3}:=R_{3}+R_{2} \\\\  & \\sim \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $B$ has $3$ pivots. In particular, the pivot columns are the $2$nd, $3$rd, and $4$th columns.",
      ":question/id": "c5080c60-4fc3-5991-80a4-8753f94201a2",
